f_yield":100.0,"_gate_int_coverage":1934.090909090909,"_gp_int_coverage":true,"_score_int_coverage":100.0,"_gate_net_debt_ebitda":-0.35961791405222415,"_gp_net_debt_ebitda":true,"_score_net_debt_ebitda":96.9,"_gate_accruals":-0.07239507261553725,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":67.4,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.13801425700983402,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":74.9,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.06896215792570978,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":false,"_score_margin_vs_hist":13.8,"_gate_piotroski":7,"_gp_piotroski":true,"_score_piotroski":77.8,"_gate_spread":-0.010157291871069077,"_gp_spread":false,"_score_spread":0.0,"_gate_roic_consistency":1.5164389354290089,"_gp_roic_consistency":false,"_score_roic_consistency":0.0,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":0.018258413790536943,"_gp_margin_advantage":false,"_score_margin_advantage":39.4,"_gate_pool_share":0.10100153700267933,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":80.4,"_gate_rev_durability":-0.00850186711970402,"_gp_rev_durability":false,"_score_rev_durability":20.7,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":0.0,"_gate_margins":0.02688645432050953,"_gp_margins":true,"_score_margins":76.9,"_gate_fund_growth":0,"_gp_fund_growth":false,"_score_fund_growth":0.0,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.013822867349587167,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":26.5,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.08635981095930301,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":100.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.009913366929600285,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":83.5,"_gate_insider_own":0.09557,"_gp_insider_own":true,"_score_insider_own":63.7,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Flexsteel Industries, Inc., together with its subsidiaries, manufactures, distributes, imports, and markets residential furniture products in the United States. The company offers stationary and motion sofas; loveseats; chairs and sectionals; bedroom furniture; dining tables and chairs; occasional and entertainment tables; and kitchen storage. It distributes its products through its e-commerce channel and direct sales force. The company was founded in 1893 and is based in Dubuque, Iowa.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Derek Paul Schmidt CPA | CEO, President & Director | Age 52 | Compensation: $1.6M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $383K ranks in the above the sector median among Consumer Cyclical peers. Each employee generates $40K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $4K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Flexsteel Industries, Inc. is a small-cap consumer cyclical business with a $311M market cap on $459M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +5% over the past three years and -1% annually across the full decade, a respectable pace for a business of this size.","Returns on capital run at 8% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests, and 22% gross margins are typical of commodity economics where competitors can replicate the product cheaply.","The business throws off $48M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 10 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.56\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 1.4%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 9.6% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.7% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $2.8M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Consumer demand is fundamentally cyclical \u2014 a recession compresses both unit volume and pricing power, and operating leverage cuts both ways.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"E-commerce margin compression and tariff exposure \u2014 digital competition erodes pricing power while trade policy reshuffles supply-chain cost structures overnight.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Brand relevance decay \u2014 shifting consumer preferences and social-media-driven trends can strand inventory and invalidate positioning faster than product cycles can adapt.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 44% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 25% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","39 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Consumer Cyclical sector outperforming the broader market over the past quarter"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Flexsteel Industries (NASDAQ:FLXS) Insider David Edward Crimmins Sells 6,100 Shares of Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/flexsteel-industries-nasdaqflx